  "description": "When one defect in a write matches more than one validation rule, the failure code follows the precedence of README section 6: a context instant that is present but not in a 4.2.1 form is 10.2.4; a non-integer ordinal is 10.2.3; an Assertion reference missing a coordinate, or a reference with an undefined @ref kind, is 10.2.4, while a well-formed reference that does not resolve is 10.2.2; @effective on a statement is 10.2.4. Each rejected write carries exactly one defect and leaves the store unchanged.",
